course: dictionary
lesson: 10416
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A word can mean different things in different places. Context tells you which meaning fits. Trinity is a good example, because it has a religious meaning and an everyday meaning.
explain: «The Trinity means one God in three persons: the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit.» The capital letter and the names Father and Son tell you this is about Christian belief. Here, Trinity is the name of a belief, not just a group of three.
explain: Now read «an unholy trinity». Unholy is the opposite of holy, so this means three bad things joined together. Check the clues, such as capital letters, names and the words around the word, before you decide which meaning fits.
fact: Trinity has two main meanings: a Christian belief, and a group of three things or people.
fact: The Trinity means one God in three persons: the Father, the Son (Jesus) and the Holy Spirit.
fact: Christians show the Trinity with symbols such as the shamrock, a little clover with three leaves on one stem.
fact: Trinity Sunday is a feast in the church year, and many churches, schools and colleges are named Trinity.
fact: A few groups that call themselves Christian do not accept the Trinity.
exercise: «The Trinity means one God in three persons.» Which meaning of Trinity is this? | A group of three friends | A shamrock with four leaves | A college for sport only | *The Christian belief in one God in three persons
exercise: «Pictures like a shamrock (a little clover with three leaves on one stem) help explain the Trinity.» What is a shamrock? | A type of green sweet | A large tree | *A little clover with three leaves on one stem | A kind of small boat
exercise: Jayden reads «an unholy trinity». What does it mean? | Three holy things together | A church service | *Three bad things joined together, said as a joke | Three shamrocks in a row
test: «Trinity Sunday» is a feast in the church year. What kind of day is it? | A day for weather forecasts | A sports day for schools | A day for shopping | *A religious feast day in the church year
test: Which word means a group of three things or people that belong closely together? | Ancient | Curt | *Trinity | Barely
exam: «A few groups that call themselves Christian do not accept the Trinity.» What does this sentence tell you? | Every Christian group believes in the Trinity | *Some groups that call themselves Christian do not accept the Trinity | Christians never go to church | The Trinity is a kind of food
